  "conclusion": {
    "decision": [
      "Retain n28.7m as the numerically strongest tokenizer endpoint under the aligned fixed-20k protocol, pending user visual review.",
      "Proceed to the separately preregistered real-environment PPO trajectory-collection experiment; do not start dynamics."
    ],
    "interpretation": [
      "The aligned endpoint supports the preregistered hypothesis: increasing from the local n16.6m architecture to the local n28.7m-label architecture improved every final EMA metric used in the comparison.",
      "The gains are modest relative to the 71.4% parameter increase, so this run establishes a capacity-quality improvement but not cost efficiency."
    ],
    "not_established": [
      "Whether users judge the n28.7m reconstructions visually acceptable.",
      "Whether the tokenizer is suitable for dynamics."
    ],
    "observed": [
      "A CPU-only architecture probe found 25,564,032 parameters for the local depth-6, d_model-384 implementation of the published 28.7M label.",
      "The first launch from source commit 3833b34 failed before any optimizer update while materializing a validation DatasetConfig that omitted a defaulted mouse_repr field.",
      "A regression test reproduced the missing-default failure before the helper was changed to materialize explicit DatasetConfig and DataloaderConfig defaults.",
      "Attempt 02 reached 1,179 recorder-confirmed completed updates before JAX reported CUDA_ERROR_STREAM_CAPTURE_INVALIDATED; no NVIDIA Xid, kernel OOM or surviving GPU process was observed.",
      "Attempt 03 restored CR-TOK-0004's own checkpoint step 0 and resumed the unchanged protocol under PID 71283.",
      "The fixed 16-clip periodic validation at 2,500 completed updates measured online clean PSNR 28.1951 dB and EMA clean PSNR 24.4368 dB on validation-set SHA256 350bd313b4f98d8bd06c06f99c029e2e5a9cb6981e3bcc5d25e9aa749b7a0188.",
      "Attempt 03 completed exactly 20,000 optimizer updates and all eight periodic validations plus four 512-clip held-out evaluations.",
      "At 20,000 updates, n28.7m EMA clean, edge and temporal-change PSNR were 36.8657, 27.0661 and 27.6592 dB.",
      "The aligned n16.6m comparison used the identical dataset path, seed, batch size, frames, batches, clip count and completed-update horizon; n28.7m improved clean, edge and temporal-change PSNR by 0.6965, 0.2921 and 0.2308 dB."
    ]
  },
